---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import CopyPrompt from '../components/CopyPrompt.astro';
import { DEPLOY_URL, DOCS, limeCta } from '../components/site';
const card = 'rounded-[12px] border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.03] p-5 sm:p-6';
const label = 'font-mono text-caption tracking-[0.14em] text-lime uppercase';
---
<Layout
  title="Install daemons.run"
  description="Install your own daemons.run control plane into your Cloudflare account, with the Deploy to Cloudflare button or your coding agent."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-12 pb-20 md:px-6 md:pt-16">
    <h1 class="text-[2.25rem] leading-[1.05] font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-[3rem]">Install <span class="text-lime">daemons.run</span></h1>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-[0.9375rem] leading-7 text-bone/75 sm:text-section sm:leading-7">
      Your control plane goes into your own Cloudflare account, at <code class="font-mono text-bone">daemons.&lt;you&gt;.workers.dev</code>. Pick one of two ways. Both take about five minutes.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5">
      <div id="deploy" class={card}>
        <p class={label}>Option 1 · In the browser</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold">Deploy to Cloudflare</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-6 text-bone/75">
          Cloudflare signs you in, copies the code to your GitHub and deploys it. It asks you for a <strong class="text-bone">setup code</strong>: any phrase you will type once, when you register your passkey.
        </p>
        <a href={DEPLOY_URL} class={`${limeCta} mt-6 w-full sm:w-auto`}>
          Deploy to Cloudflare <Icon name="arrow" size={16} />
        </a>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[0.875rem] leading-6 text-bone/65">Then open your new Worker URL, enter the setup code and register a passkey.</p>
      </div>

      <div id="agent" class={card}>
        <p class={label}>Option 2 · With your coding agent</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold">Ask Claude Code or Codex</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-6 text-bone/75">
          Paste this into a coding agent on your computer. It clones the repository, signs in to Cloudflare (you approve in the browser) and gives you a setup link.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5"><CopyPrompt /></div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[0.875rem] leading-6 text-bone/65">
          The agent follows <a href="/install.md" class="text-bone underline decoration-bone/30 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-bone">install.md</a>. You can follow it yourself, too.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class={card}>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">What you need</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-6 text-bone/80">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><Icon name="check" size={20} class="mt-0.5 text-lime" /><span>A <strong class="text-bone">Cloudflare account</strong>. The free plan is enough for normal use.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><Icon name="check" size={20} class="mt-0.5 text-lime" /><span>A <strong class="text-bone">Hetzner account</strong> for servers (from €5.49/month, billed by Hetzner), <strong class="text-bone">or any Ubuntu 24.04 machine</strong> you can run one command on.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><Icon name="check" size={20} class="mt-0.5 text-lime" /><span>A device with a passkey: your phone, laptop or security key.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 text-[0.875rem] text-bone/65">
      Questions or problems? Read the <a href={DOCS} class="text-bone underline decoration-bone/30 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-bone">docs on GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
